Give a repository's Git token its own switch on Settings → Repository variables.

A repository's Git token is its GIT_TOKEN variable
(images/server/patches/0010-repo-git-token.patch). The page shows it apart from
the other variables: the card lists "Git token" instead of GIT_TOKEN, and the
editor has a Git token switch with a write-only field, where a blank field keeps
the stored token and switching it off removes it. A GIT_TOKEN typed as a
variable name is refused, and one in a pasted .env fills the field.
Base: omnigent v0.15.0 (c8b9b85f822f), after 0001-0011.

